            0.117,
            0.426,
            0.663,
            0.447
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "14.6.1 Guesstimates: Did You Ever Wonder?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.459,
            0.883,
            0.575
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Guesstimate questions are problems in which you make a reasonable estimate for a quantity when exact data are not available. Instead of finding a perfectly accurate answer, you use assumptions, approximations, logic, and everyday knowledge to model a given situation and arrive at a sensible estimate. Do you remember solving such questions in earlier grades?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.58,
            0.574,
            0.733
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 5:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Lallan’s golgappa (a small hollow ball made of wheat) stall has a cylindrical vessel with pani (spiced water) in it. The vessel is of radius 10 cm and it has pani up to a height of 50 cm. Estimate the number of golgappas he can serve assuming all golgappas are spheres. Before calculating, make a guess."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.591,
            0.58,
            0.875,
            0.745
          ],
          "content": [
